From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:25:20 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 40/66] Meridian: security hardening from the audits

- Agent server: no use-after-free when a line closes its connection; caps on
  line size, connections and pending output.
- Agents reach only web pages (no chrome://, Workbench or file:); uploads are
  copied after approval, never re-read from the original path.
- Test switches only work for a profile in the temp folder.
- Updater: checksums trusted only under the Ed25519 release signature; safe
  zip entries; the staged app must be the version it claims; the signature
  is checked again before the swap.
- Downloads: Safe Browsing verdicts shown; keeping a dangerous file asks in a
  native dialog.
- Hosts are cut on the left so the registrable domain always shows.
- CLI agents run under sandbox-exec; page fetcher refuses non-public hosts.
- Workbench: terminal fd ownership, sandbox state per profile, no symlinks
  followed out of a project, secret files guarded, vault files created 0600.

